From fac858c175214d33f5f288028cd8c02fa13bb864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konstantinos Papadimitriou
 <konstantinos.papadimitriou_ext@softathome.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Aug 2024 11:39:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Several fixes to avoid creating too many subprocesses making
 the plugin unresponsive.

Problem: After the last commit, time-manager used to create too many
subproccesses calling chronyc with high timeout values. This caused the plugin
to become unresponsive when the chrony daemon failed to respond in time. At the
same time mop tests started to fail because after changing the DM the chronyd
config wasn't properly reapplied.

Solution: Instead of trying to manually re-apply the config file each time
something changes in the DM or in the uplink interface's state, restart it
properly at each DM change and only reload the ntp sources when the interface
state changes.

Issue: HOP-6722 [PrplOs][tr181-time] Time.Status takes more than 90secs to get Synchronized state at startup. [fix]
Issue: HOP-7294 [time] cpu usage of chrony 38.6% / unbound 48.8% when wan is down [fix]
Issue: HOP-7261 [regression][time] automated test started failing [fix]
Issue: HOP-7286 [PRPL][4.0.16.8][System > Date & Time, Automatic Time Update]Changing time zone or Enabling/Disabling Automatic Time Update > Displays 'Something went wrong' [fix]
